  "id": "stabilizing-selection",
  "term": "stabilizing selection",
  "definition": "Stabilizing selection is a pattern in which environmental stress favors survival of individuals with a particular phenotype, while those showing less stable development are less fit. At the population level, this tends to narrow the range of observed traits.",
